A||||4||Seanh||Engine Compartment Insulation||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||10-07-2000||10:21 AM||||I have been working on my engine for a couple weeks now and got to noticing how badly the insulation back there is falling apart and looks nasty. I am going to pull the engine from the car this Jan or Feb to rebuild the car, and I was just wondering if there is any place that sell some new replacment insulation for the engine bay? If no, what could I use to replace it? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||10-07-2000||10:39 AM||||Unless you want to keep the original look, you can just take off the pieces on the sides of the engine compartment (around the strut towers) without affecting the sound level inside the car.  Leave the piece on the firewall unless you like hearing more of your engine while you drive  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Not having the stuff on the sides makes it much easier to keep the engine bay clean.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||10-07-2000||10:46 AM||||About the only good use for that insulation is to hold water in and help the sides rust out...  The engine compartment looks much cleaner w/o it.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||10-07-2000||12:11 PM||||Ok thanks. I have a stereo system in the car, so I cant have any more engine noise in there. I was think though, I am going to rebuilt the car pretty soon, and I will have to remove the interior. Could I just remove the insulation from the engine bay and add more sound insulation on the inside of the firewall behind the seats? Or maybe I should just clean up the firewall insulation and reuse it. I was hopeing that I could remove the sides without any trouble. Thanks <P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||10-07-2000||01:04 PM||||no reason u cant put it in front of firewall, behind seats, u got 5 or 6 inches of space to fill up behind the seats. The stuff in engine compt is usless junk anyway.||||reg||1
